IN THE COURT OF THE LEARNED SESSIONS JUDGE, JAIPUR

Sessions Case No. ______ of 2025

State of Rajasthan                                    … Prosecution

Versus

Vijay Kumar Sharma                                       … Accused / Applicant

APPLICATION UNDER SECTION 227 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023
FOR DISCHARGE OF THE ACCUSED

MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:

1. That the applicant is innocent and has been falsely implicated in the present case.

2. That the prosecution has filed a chargesheet under Sections 420, 406, 409 and 120B of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.

3. That the case is essentially a civil dispute dressed as a criminal case. The applicant had genuine business setbacks and made repayment efforts.

4. GROUNDS FOR DISCHARGE

A. There is no evidence of dishonest intention at the inception of the loan transaction. The applicant genuinely intended to repay the loan.

B. The documents submitted to the bank were genuine. The allegation of forgery is based on misinterpretation by the bank.

C. The diversion of funds was due to genuine business exigencies and not with dishonest intention.

D. The applicant made several repayment attempts, which show his bona fides.

E. The matter is essentially a civil dispute between the bank and the borrower. Civil remedies are available.

F. Even if the entire prosecution material is taken at its face value, no prima facie case under Sections 420, 406, 409 is made out.

5. That the Supreme Court has held that where the dispute is essentially civil, criminal proceedings should not be encouraged.

6. That continuing the criminal proceedings against the applicant would be an abuse of the process of law.

PRAYER

It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:

(a) Discharge the applicant from the charges under Sections 420, 406, 409 and 120B of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023;
(b) Pass any other order as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.

